.TH GO-MCP-JSONRPC 7 "2026-10-20" "go-mcp @VERSION@" "Go MCP Framework"
.SH NAME
go-mcp-jsonrpc \- JSON-RPC 2.0 messages, a connection and a framed stream
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
import "code.linenisgreat.com/purse-first/libs/go-mcp/jsonrpc"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B jsonrpc
package provides the JSON-RPC 2.0 message types used by the rest of
go-mcp (the
.B server
and
.B transport
packages exchange
.B *jsonrpc.Message
values), plus a small bidirectional connection type that frames messages
with
.B Content-Length
headers in the style of the Language Server Protocol.
MCP stdio servers use newline-delimited JSON instead; see
.BR go-mcp-transport (7).
.SH TYPES
.SS Message
.nf
type Message struct {
    JSONRPC string          // always Version ("2.0")
    ID      *ID
    Method  string
    Params  json.RawMessage
    Result  json.RawMessage
    Error   *Error
}
.fi
.PP
A message is classified by its fields:
.IP \(bu 2
.B IsRequest
reports an ID and a method.
.IP \(bu 2
.B IsNotification
reports a method and no ID.
.IP \(bu 2
.B IsResponse
reports an ID and no method.
.PP
Constructors marshal their argument with encoding/json and return an error
if that fails:
.nf
func NewRequest(id ID, method string, params any) (*Message, error)
func NewNotification(method string, params any) (*Message, error)
func NewResponse(id ID, result any) (*Message, error)
func NewErrorResponse(id ID, code int, message string,
    data any) (*Message, error)
.fi
.SS ID
A request identifier that is a number, a string or null.
.nf
func NewNumberID(n int64) ID
func NewStringID(s string) ID
func (id ID) IsNull() bool
.fi
.PP
Unmarshaling accepts a JSON number, string or null and rejects anything
else.
.SS Error
.nf
type Error struct {
    Code    int
    Message string
    Data    json.RawMessage
}
.fi
.PP
.B *Error
implements the
.B error
interface.
.SS Error codes
The package defines the JSON-RPC 2.0 codes
.BR ParseError " (-32700),"
.BR InvalidRequest " (-32600),"
.BR MethodNotFound " (-32601),"
.BR InvalidParams " (-32602) and"
.BR InternalError " (-32603),"
and three further codes:
.BR ServerNotInitialized " (-32002),"
.BR RequestCancelled " (-32800) and"
.BR ContentModified " (-32801)."
.SS Stream
Reads and writes messages framed by a
.B Content-Length
header, a blank line and the JSON body.
.nf
func NewStream(r io.Reader, w io.Writer) *Stream
func (s *Stream) Read() (*Message, error)
func (s *Stream) Write(msg *Message) error
.fi
.PP
.B Read
fails if the header is malformed or has no
.BR Content-Length .
.B Write
is safe for concurrent use.
.SS Conn
A bidirectional connection over a
.BR Stream .
.nf
type Handler func(ctx context.Context, msg *Message) (*Message, error)

func NewConn(r io.Reader, w io.Writer, handler Handler) *Conn
func (c *Conn) Run(ctx context.Context) error
func (c *Conn) Call(ctx context.Context, method string,
    params any) (json.RawMessage, error)
func (c *Conn) Notify(method string, params any) error
func (c *Conn) Reply(id ID, result any) error
func (c *Conn) ReplyError(id ID, code int, message string,
    data any) error
func (c *Conn) NextID() ID
func (c *Conn) Close() error
.fi
.PP
.B Run
reads messages until the stream fails.
A response is delivered to the pending
.B Call
with the same ID.
Every other message is passed to the handler in its own goroutine;
a non-nil response from the handler is written back.
If the handler returns an error for a request, the connection replies
with an
.B InternalError
response carrying the error text.
.PP
.B Call
sends a request with an ID from
.B NextID
and waits for the response.
It returns the response's result, the response's
.B *Error
if it carries one, or the context's error if the context ends first.
.PP
.B Close
only marks the connection closed.
It does not close the underlying reader or writer.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR go-mcp (7),
.BR go-mcp-server (7),
.BR go-mcp-transport (7)
